  s8: `Added 12-element counter-case: customer financing friction on THOWs prices buyers out (chattel 7.5-13.5% APR over 7-15 years on $95K THOW = $1,150-$1,850/month, deals collapse at financing step costing 4-12 weeks per dead deal, pre-qualify BEFORE build with Rock Solid / Lightstream / 21st Mortgage / KOA Finance / Mountain America lender partners and 35-50% non-refundable deposit); zoning resistance for THOWs and container homes kills siting (most US municipalities classify THOWs as RVs for RV park / campground placement only, ADUs streamlined in CA/OR/WA/CO/MN/NY/MA but prohibited in most other states, container homes face worst zoning resistance with many jurisdictions explicitly prohibiting); tariff and material cost volatility 22-65% 2020-2026 per Random Lengths Lumber Composite Index / CME Lumber Futures / BLS Producer Price Index crushes fixed-price contracts without escalation clauses (include materials escalation clause above 10% threshold); warranty callback economics erode delivered margin (8-22% of units have warranty issues in first 12 months, budget 3-6% warranty reserve, structure 12-month limited workmanship warranty plus manufacturer pass-throughs, document delivery with photos plus inspection checklist plus customer signoff); skilled labor shortage limits production (BLS construction employment up 12-18% 2020-2026 with under 4% unemployment in skilled trades, 6-12% annual wage growth, partner with trade schools ABC / AGC / Job Corps / community colleges); custom-build margin erosion through scope creep destroys profitability (menu-based customization with 3-5 standard model lines plus defined upgrades, change orders require written documentation plus signature plus payment before work); seasonality and weather delays for site-built ADU in cold-weather climates (8-22 weeks/year weather delays in PNW / Northeast / Midwest / Rockies, schedule with contingency); cash conversion cycle and working capital intensity (35-65% working capital exposure per unit during 6-24 week build, maintain progress payment structure 20-35% deposit + 25-30% framing + 25-30% finish + 15-20% delivery plus 3-6 months operating reserve plus working capital line of credit); OSHA safety burden real (construction highest occupational fatality rate per BLS Census of Fatal Occupational Injuries, OSHA Fatal Four falls / electrocutions / struck-by-objects / caught-in-between account for 60%+ of fatalities, written safety program plus weekly toolbox talks plus PPE plus harness/fall-protection above 6 feet plus OSHA 10 or 30 hour training); subcontractor classification trap (DOL 2024 Final Rule, IRS 20-factor, CA AB5, subcontractors 1099 only if truly independent business with own tools / insurance / license / multiple customers / pricing autonomy, misclassification audits $50K-$250K+ back-tax penalties have closed operators, in-house carpenters and helpers W-2 always); venture-funded prefab cautionary tales Katerra 2021 shutdown $2B raised and Veev 2023 shutdown $585M+ raised demonstrate construction does not scale like software (physical jobsite constraints / weather / supplier coordination / skilled labor scarcity / customer customization / local-permitting reality resist software-product-style scaling); adjacent businesses may fit better (traditional residential remodeling lower complexity, framing subcontractor lower capital, cabinet shop specialty without GC scope, garage / shop building simpler product, traditional manufactured housing dealer Clayton/Cavco/Skyline established infrastructure, ADU-specialty in streamlined-state only, accessory structure shed/studio/workshop simpler permitting) — with honest 13-condition verdict on who should and should not start.`,
